; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 10, course 5 "Kite Hill": "Kite Hill" (SPEC.md 137.20)
;
; D major in 6/8 at 121 to the dotted quarter: a 16th is a row, and the rows
; alternate five and four sub-ticks (`groove 5 4`), so an 8th is always 9 and
; a bar of six 8ths is 54 sub-ticks, 0.99 s. A pattern is FOUR bars, 3.96 s.
; No other course song is in compound time (Windmill Lane is a 3/4 waltz).
;
; The course is wind carrying a ball up a hill, so the tune FLOATS and RISES.
; REVISED after the owner's first listen ("the first 4-5 seconds are good, but
; then it repeats too much for too long"): the first version stated its arc
; four times, a step higher each time, in one rhythm; this one states it ONCE
; and then develops. Its MOTIF is a kite let out on its string and dipping
; back: up a broken chord in the 6/8's long-short lilt, through the RAISED
; FOURTH (G#, the lydian's "air"), to the top, and down the chord again:
;   a4 >d8 f+4 g+8 | a4. f+4 d8                    (over D)
;
; A  (8 bars): the motif, then an ANSWER in another rhythm (a held note, a
;    turn of 8ths, a close on D); then a leap to a held D6, a run, and a
;    whole-bar E6 over A, a half close. D D A7 D | G A G A.
; B  (8 bars): the SECOND THEME, in B minor and an octave lower: two slow
;    notes a bar against a bar of quick ones, and the harp changes from its
;    long-short-long to three even quarters across the bar (a hemiola), the
;    hats with it. Bm Bm Em A | Bm A D A.
; C  (4 bars): the THERMAL, a bridge: up an E7 chord to an E6 held a bar and
;    a third, the glide down A7. E7 A A7 D.
; A' (8 bars): the motif comes back a sixth HIGHER and turned round (from
;    F#, to a held F#6, the summit, by a run of six 8ths), and closes for the
;    first time on a whole bar of D. D D G D | A7 G A7 D.
; D  (8 bars): the GLIDE: falling notes that quicken, then THE GUST - a run
;    up six 16ths through the raised fourth that STOPS DEAD on a clipped
;    note, the harp stopping with it - and a bar's BREATH, harp alone.
;    G D Em A7 | G D E7 A7.
; Intro (the harp alone, the gust, the breath), A B C A' D for ever: the loop
; is 9 patterns, 36 bars, 35.6 s. Its 36 bars have 14 different rhythms (the
; first version's 40 had 10), no two-bar phrase has the rhythm of the one
; before it (7 of 19 did), and none is the one before it moved up (6 were).
;
; THE SPEAKER: the lead carries it, and `spkbass` gives the harp's broken
; chord to every rest of the lead: the two bars before the tune, the breath
; after the gust, the half bars that end B and C. Only the kick blips (every
; two bars, on a phrase's first note; none under the gust or the thermal);
; the hats are the AdLib's. No arpeggio macro and no vibrato is written.
; ON THE ADLIB the recorder sings over the harp and a soft string pad whose
; chords all sit BELOW the tune (First Roll's lesson), and the chip's own
; vibrato is on the held notes.

song kitehill "Kite Hill"
groove 5 4
unit 16
rows 48
measure 12
spkbass
voice lead recorder
voice bass harp
voice chord strings

; --- the intro (as the owner heard it): the harp, the gust, the breath, D D E7 A7 --
lead LI = r2. | r2. | v13 o5 q0 e16 f+16 g+16 a16 b16 >c+16 q5 d8 r4 | r2. |
bass BI = v13 o3 d4 a8 >f+4. | <d4 b8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 r4. | <a4 >g8 >c+4. |
chord CI = v10 o3 [a >d f+]2.^2. | [g+ b >d]2. | [g >c+ e]2. |

; --- A: the motif and its answer; the leap, the run and the half close -------------
lead LN1 = v13 o4 a4 >d8 f+4 g+8 | a4. f+4 d8 | e4. g8 f+8 e8 | d4 <a8 >d4. |
lead LN2 = v13 o5 d4 b8 >d4. | c+8 d8 e8 <a4. | b4 >c+8 d8 e8 f+8 | e2. |
bass BN1 = v13 o3 d4 a8 >f+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <<a4 >g8 >c+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. |
bass BN2 = v13 o3 g4 >d8 b4. | <<a4 >e8 >c+4. | <g4 >d8 b4. | <<a4 >e8 >c+4. |
chord CN1 = v10 o3 [a >d f+]2.^2. | [g >c+ e]2. | [a >d f+]2. |
chord CN2 = v10 o3 [g b >d]2. | [a >c+ e]2. | [g b >d]2. | [a >c+ e]2. |

; --- B: the second theme, B minor, lower; the harp in three even quarters ----------
lead LM1 = v13 o5 f+4. b4. | a8 b8 a8 f+4 d8 | e4. g4. | f+8 e8 d8 c+4. |
lead LM2 = v13 o5 d4 f+8 b4 >d8 | c+4. <a4 e8 | f+4 g8 a4 b8 | a4. r4. |
bass BM1 = v13 o2 b4 >f+4 >d4 | <<b4 >f+4 >d4 | <e4 b4 >g4 | <<a4 >e4 >c+4 |
bass BM2 = v13 o2 b4 >f+4 >d4 | <<a4 >e4 >c+4 | <d4 a4 >f+4 | <<a4 >e4 >c+4 |
chord CM1 = v10 o3 [f+ b >d]2.^2. | [g b >e]2. | [a >c+ e]2. |
chord CM2 = v10 o3 [f+ b >d]2. | [a >c+ e]2. | [a >d f+]2. | [a >c+ e]2. |

; --- C: the thermal. Up the E7 chord, the E held a bar and a third, down A7 --------
lead LA3 = v13 o5 e4 g+8 b4 >d8 | e2.&e4 c+8 <a4 g8 | f+4. r4. |
bass BA3 = v13 o3 e4 b8 >g+4. | <a4 >e8 >c+4. | <<<a4 >g8 >c+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. |
chord CA3 = v10 o3 [g+ b >d]2. | [a >c+ e]2. | [g >c+ e]2. | [a >d f+]2. |

; --- A': the motif a sixth higher and turned round; the summit; the full close -----
lead LR1 = v13 o5 f+4 a8 >d4 e8 | f+4. d4 <a8 | b8 >c+8 d8 e8 f+8 g8 | f+2. |
lead LR2 = v13 o6 e4 c+8 <a4 >c+8 | d4. <b4. | g4 e8 c+4 e8 | d2. |
bass BR1 = v13 o3 d4 a8 >f+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <g4 >d8 b4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. |
bass BR2 = v13 o2 a4 >g8 >c+4. | <g4 >d8 b4. | <<a4 >g8 >c+4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. |
chord CR1 = v10 o3 [a >d f+]2.^2. | [g b >d]2. | [a >d f+]2. |
chord CR2 = v10 o3 [g >c+ e]2. | [g b >d]2. | [g >c+ e]2. | [a >d f+]2. |

; --- D: the glide, quickening; then the gust and the breath ------------------------
lead LD1 = v13 o6 d4. <b4. | a4 f+8 d4 f+8 | g8 e8 <b8 >e4. | c+4 e8 a4. |
lead LB2 = v13 o6 e4 d8 <b4 g8 | f+4 a8 >d4. |
           q0 <e16 f+16 g+16 a16 b16 >c+16 q5 d8 r4 | r2. |
bass BB1 = v13 o3 g4 >d8 b4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 >g4. | <<a4 >g8 >c+4. |
bass BB2 = v13 o3 g4 >d8 b4. | <d4 a8 >f+4. | <e4 b8 r4. | <a4 >g8 >c+4. |
chord CB1 = v10 o3 [g b >d]2. | [a >d f+]2. | [g b >e]2. | [g >c+ e]2. |
chord CB2 = v10 o3 [g b >d]2. | [a >d f+]2. | [g+ b >d]2. | [g >c+ e]2. |

; the beat: a kick every two bars and the hats' long-short. The gust and the
; breath are bare (a kick there blipped over the run's first note on the
; speaker), and under the thermal the third bar has no kick, so the speaker
; holds the E unbroken. In B the hats go in three with the harp.
drum DA = k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 |
drum DB = k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | r1. |
drum DT = k4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 | h4 h8 h4 h8 |
drum DH = k4 h4 h4 | h4 h4 h4 | k4 h4 h4 | h4 h4 h4 |

order LI  BI  CI  DB          ; 0: the intro, D D E7 A7
order LN1 BN1 CN1 DA          ; 1: A   D D A7 D - the loop comes back here
order LN2 BN2 CN2 DA          ; 2:     G A G A, the half close
order LM1 BM1 CM1 DH          ; 3: B   Bm Bm Em A
order LM2 BM2 CM2 DH          ; 4:     Bm A D A
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DT          ; 5: C   E7 A A7 D, the thermal
order LR1 BR1 CR1 DA          ; 6: A'  D D G D, the summit
order LR2 BR2 CR2 DA          ; 7:     A7 G A7 D, the full close
order LD1 BB1 CB1 DA          ; 8: D   G D Em A7, the glide
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB          ; 9:     G D E7 A7, the gust and the breath
loop 1
